      "id": "t002370",
      "source": "Multiply map length by the scale denominator, then convert units. A scale is a ratio, not an added distance.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002371",
      "source": "Task.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002372",
      "source": "What is the real straight-line distance in kilometres?",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002373",
      "source": "Step-by-step solution.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002374",
      "source": "1. Real centimetres=5×50000=250000. 2. Convert to kilometres: 250000÷100,000=2.5.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002375",
      "source": "Answer.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002376",
      "source": "2.5 km.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002377",
      "source": "Knowledge takeaway.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002378",
      "source": "Scale problems are ratio problems: keep units explicit and conversion becomes mechanical.",
      "translation": ""
