      "id": "t002415",
      "source": "N2. Coordinates and constraint-based location",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002416",
      "source": "Problem 131. Locating a point by constraints: case 1",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002417",
      "source": "Knowledge context.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002418",
      "source": "Coordinates turn location into numbers. Multiple spatial clues can be treated as simultaneous constraints.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002419",
      "source": "Given facts.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002420",
      "source": "A point P lies on an integer grid with x,y from 0 to 5. It satisfies x+y=2 and x−y=0.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002421",
      "source": "Rules.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002422",
      "source": "A location is valid only if it satisfies every stated equation and inequality at the same time.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002423",
      "source": "Task.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002424",
      "source": "Which coordinate(s) can P occupy? Is the solution unique?",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002425",
      "source": "Step-by-step solution.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002426",
      "source": "1. List pairs satisfying x+y=2. 2. Keep only those also satisfying x−y=0. 3. The remaining set is [(1, 1)].",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002427",
      "source": "Answer.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002428",
      "source": "P=(1, 1); the solution is unique.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002429",
      "source": "Knowledge takeaway.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002430",
      "source": "A constraint problem is solved by satisfying all conditions together, not one at a time independently.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002431",
      "source": "Formal model.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t002432",
      "source": "Constraint satisfaction over integer pairs (x,y).",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
